WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.923
- The thing
(upbeat ambient music)

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:03.490
that has kept me in a very strong position

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:06.490
from the earliest wine videos I made

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.530
to what I'm gonna do tomorrow

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:13.530
is I have never talked about
something I don't know, ever.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.520
First of all, it's a real pleasure.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:21.340
I think content creation
and all of you are in it

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.570
so a lot of this stuff will make sense,

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.660
but I think the first thing
that I think about always

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.370
is self awareness.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.930
I think the biggest issue
for content creators

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:36.750
is them being inspired by someone else,

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.440
and then them subconsciously,
not even consciously,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.900
subconsciously trying
to be like that person,

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.600
which is an incredibly difficult task

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.390
because every one of us
in this room, me included,

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.130
have strength and weaknesses

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.520
in their ability to create content.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.928
So I think there's a couple
things to think about,

00:00:56.928 --> 00:01:00.140
one, your own self-awareness
of what you're good at.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.360
For example, I'll give you one,

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.230
I think the concept of writing content

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.060
is like forgotten in a visual world,

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.880
yet, I can tell you

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.840
that some of my written
content on LinkedIn

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.820
is dramatically more profound

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.450
and does well than my clips
on TikTok or Instagram.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.310
And there may be people in this room

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:25.220
whose strongest method of communication

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.010
is actually in written form,

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:32.010
yet, the push towards
short form video or images

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.850
make them work on that

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.890
when they're deviating from a strength.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.950
So I think first and foremost

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.260
what I think about is a couple things

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:46.030
and they're all in the
form of transparency

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.130
and self-awareness,

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:50.050
one, what are you best at communicating?

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.170
Is it audio, video, written form?

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.170
Two, the thing that has kept
me in a very strong position

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.830
from the earliest wine videos I made

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.880
to what I'm gonna do tomorrow

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.880
is I have never talked about
something I don't know, ever.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:11.580
I think when you're a content creator,

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.193
you feel pressured to output.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.320
And when you feel pressured to output,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.250
you can get very caught to start talking

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.410
or creating around something
you may not fully understand.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.200
A lot of people come and go

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.880
and there's some very clear
truths to having success.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.360
And I think it's one,
understanding your format,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.850
while still trying to challenge yourself.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.670
You may be better at writing,

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.980
it's still good to try
to be better at video,

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.830
but it's not crippling yourself

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.800
and thinking you can only be
successful if you do video.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.310
Two, do not deviate from your knowledge.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.130
Now that doesn't mean
going, like look at me,

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.780
I'm talking about NFTs.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.460
I spent a 100 hours of research

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.560
before I made my first video,

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.610
but putting in the work

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.753
to be able to talk about
something new is very important.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:07.950
The quickest way I've seen people lose

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.370
is by being too quick to talk
about things they don't know.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.210
Very important.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.970
Number three,

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.600
a very big thing for everybody
to keep in mind here,

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.513
do not fall in love with the
platform that got you there.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.110
A very big thing that
I've seen consistently

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.470
in the last 15 years

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.090
is Twitter was your strong
platform, here came Instagram,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:33.430
and you didn't want
Instagram to become big

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:34.910
because you didn't wanna start over

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.540
and build up your following count.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.270
So many, and this is gonna
make sense for all of you,

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:43.430
so many leaders on Instagram
made a huge mistake

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.330
by not adopting TikTok, right?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.113
They didn't want to 'cause
they had all their followers,

00:03:49.113 --> 00:03:53.860
constant mistake being too
romantic about platform

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.893
and not adjusting to where the
attention is actually going.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.533
Those are some themes that I
would give a lot of thought to.

00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:02.180
- I think one of the
things we focus a lot on

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.337
is writing as well.

00:04:04.337 --> 00:04:07.522
So we're trying to teach teams
that really scripting out

00:04:07.522 --> 00:04:10.303
to storytell before they create content.

00:04:10.303 --> 00:04:14.681
So that definitely goes in
line with what you said.

00:04:14.681 --> 00:04:16.544
Platforms a little bit more.

00:04:16.544 --> 00:04:17.750
How do you manage that?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.490
I mean, it's a lot of work
to be on six platforms.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.480
Especially when you are starting out.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.280
How do you recommend they do this?

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:27.480
- You know, the way you do it
is a couple different ways,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.500
one, I think that a lot of people get hurt

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.460
by the ideology of perfection.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.400
So I think one of the reasons
long before I had DRock

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.910
or a team, I was able to by
myself while running businesses,

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.110
be active on every platform

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.710
is because I didn't ideologically

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:48.740
think about every single piece of content.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.810
I think when you're
trying to make every piece

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.840
perfect for yourself,

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:57.840
perfection is usually just
another word for insecurity.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.350
You know, everyone's overthinking it.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:04.492
And so one, it's to feel
comfortable with that,

00:05:04.492 --> 00:05:09.492
number two, is to be okay with
not being on six platforms.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.070
You know, I think sometimes

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.820
we feel too much pressure
to be everywhere,

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.650
I talk about it, like be
everywhere, post a lot.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.460
A lot of people can't
manage that and that's okay.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.110
I believe it has to do
with insecurity of success

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.170
of the piece of content.

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:28.480
The biggest reason people
didn't go to TikTok

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.550
when they were winning on Instagram

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.890
was they didn't have the
humility and the self confidence

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.683
to not be successful
on TikTok immediately.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:40.910
So I think the biggest
reason people don't produce

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.060
is more of a mental game than,

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.160
it's not hard to produce
content for six platforms.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.510
It's really not.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:48.937
You can do it.

00:05:48.937 --> 00:05:53.937
It's that people fear
lack of success in numbers

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.750
from a vanity standpoint,

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.520
which stopped them from actually doing it.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.520
So I think humility, humility
is one of the true superpowers

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.500
of a scaled influencer or content creator,

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.540
being okay with starting at zero

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:14.563
or being okay if the
content's not doing great.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.103
Super.
- I'll give you another,

00:06:17.103 --> 00:06:18.720
I mean, for example with me on TikTok,

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.850
even though I know it's the
most important platform,

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.830
I don't have the time to
produce original TikToks,

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.790
so I know my post produced content

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:29.120
doesn't maximize my
ability to win on TikTok,

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.130
but I'd rather still put out stuff

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.720
and get what I can

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.990
than be insecure

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.580
that I'm only getting
50,000 views on a TikTok

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.120
when I have 13 million followers,

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.210
that doesn't register to me as a negative,

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.075
for too many people it does
register as a negative.

00:06:43.075 --> 00:06:44.783
- There's still a lot of people over here

00:06:44.783 --> 00:06:46.053
that are reluctant to move into TikTok.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.216
We still have that around here.

00:06:49.216 --> 00:06:50.718
Is that the case globally than?

00:06:50.718 --> 00:06:52.340
- It's the case globally.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.793
It's a huge mistake.

00:06:54.685 --> 00:06:56.210
TikTok is eating up the attention

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.940
of the consumer by the second,

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:02.650
to be a content creator,
like to be in this room

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.740
and to not be producing content for TikTok

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.773
is virtually unacceptable.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.580
I mean, if you're a content producer,

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.460
that's just a,

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.790
especially all the
different ways that TikTok

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.440
now makes it easy to make
content, voiceovers, image,

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:22.440
like there's, you're also
making a very important mistake

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.870
if you're not doing it.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:28.590
TikTok is based on the interest graph,

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.050
not on the social graph.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.951
What I mean by that is
as many of you know,

00:07:33.951 --> 00:07:38.100
TikTok puts content in front of you

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.953
based on what you're interested
in, not who you follow.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.520
This is a very important
insight for everybody here,

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.730
as AI and algorithms continue to increase,

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:51.330
that is a much stickier
way of doing content

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.853
than following people.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.303
By not making TikToks right now,

00:07:56.303 --> 00:07:59.000
you are not getting the practice

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.990
of understanding the interest graph,

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.921
which would 100%

00:08:02.921 --> 00:08:06.640
going to be the way the
next platform is built.

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:11.490
And so you're not getting
accustomed to that format

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.710
which is almost like not
running on a treadmill

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.680
before you have to run a marathon.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.960
So another reason TikTok
is incredibly important

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.960
is it's prepping you
for the next iteration,

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.230
and by not doing it,

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.210
you're getting even further
behind as a content creator

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:28.043
because your brain

00:08:28.043 --> 00:08:31.070
starts going into interest graph creation,

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.250
which is very important.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:37.070
So when TikTok was first popping
and I was making content,

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.930
'cause I was making content
when it was musically

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.720
before even the TikTok acquisition,

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.110
a lot of people are
like, what are you doing?

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:45.770
This is for 13 year old girls dancing.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:48.320
And I'm like, it's not, it is now,

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.810
but Facebook was only for college kids,

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.460
and Instagram was just for photographers.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.795
Platforms evolve.

00:08:54.795 --> 00:08:56.070
I think that,

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:59.580
yes, it's important to be
contextual to the platform,

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:03.970
but not at the expense
of your authenticity.

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:05.320
So I'd rather you deliver

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:09.650
the way you would deliver on
Twitter and LinkedIn on TikTok

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.129
and let the chips fall where they may,

00:09:12.129 --> 00:09:15.730
than for you to not be who you are.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:20.290
At the same token, there
is very much creative ways

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:24.580
to deliver serious information on TikTok.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:29.580
And I think there are
countless examples of that.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.610
And so I think that,

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:35.120
yes, I think you should be
contextual to a platform,

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:38.804
but not at the expense of the content.

00:09:38.804 --> 00:09:39.637
- Gotcha.

00:09:39.637 --> 00:09:41.010
- You don't have to dumb it down.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.665
- Yeah.
- You have to make it

00:09:42.665 --> 00:09:43.751
contextual to TikTok.

00:09:43.751 --> 00:09:45.751
- We talk a lot about diversify revenue.

00:09:46.775 --> 00:09:48.871
What kind of advice would
you have for the guys

00:09:48.871 --> 00:09:49.954
in terms of diversifying

00:09:49.954 --> 00:09:52.060
straight out of the gates right now?

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.053
- To do it.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:59.330
Diversifying your income streams
is always a good strategy.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.764
- Oh, it's not?

00:10:00.764 --> 00:10:02.517
- Is always a good strategy.
- Always a good strategy,

00:10:02.517 --> 00:10:03.350
yeah.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:04.308
- Of course.
- Gotcha.

00:10:04.308 --> 00:10:05.260
- Now having the capacity

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:08.420
or back to some of the subjects
that you just mentioned,

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.050
some individuals here

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.510
content is more conducive
to other revenue streams.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.680
If you've got a health
and wellness platform,

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:21.620
it's easier for you to sell
a health and wellness product

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.430
than let's say being a doctor.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.750
Like, but subscription
products of premium content

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.440
is always in play for people
that I think a lot of people

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:33.473
don't think about instantaneously.

00:10:33.473 --> 00:10:37.630
But yeah, I mean, in creating
as many revenue streams

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.617
as possible is always a good idea,

00:10:40.617 --> 00:10:45.000
the problem is, it's back
to content and platform.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.350
You have to actually be decent at it.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.500
Like if you're gonna sell a product,

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.530
the product needs to be good

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.010
or you're not gonna have repeat business

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.660
and that's not a viable business.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.690
So I think, you know, we started with this

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.993
and I'll bring it up again with revenue,

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:02.037
self-awareness is very important.

00:11:02.037 --> 00:11:04.500
You know, if you don't have any passion

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.023
for creating a product,

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:10.177
well, then it's probably a
bad idea to create a product.

00:11:10.177 --> 00:11:11.433
- Hmm.
- And so I think,

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:17.430
but yes, I mean, I think
relying on brand deals is fine

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:19.560
because there's so many businesses

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:22.270
and there'll potentially
always be opportunities,

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:26.650
but the more you can control
it, the more interesting it is,

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:28.200
which is why I think so many creators

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.990
eventually go to their own product.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:32.840
One of the things as
creators we think about is,

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.620
how do we sustain for
a long period of time

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.080
because people may get bored?

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.530
There's many different
ways to talk about this.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:43.530
First of all, I once took
a two and a half year gap

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:48.150
of producing any content,
two and a half years.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:52.153
So for five years, I did wine
content from 2006 to 2011

00:11:52.153 --> 00:11:56.890
and then in 2014 I started
the #AskGaryVee Show.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:58.550
That's a long gap.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.010
So I think a lot of times
we beat each other up,

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:04.430
you beat yourself up for
not producing content.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:08.630
I'm potentially one of the
most prolific content creators

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:12.220
of the last decade, and I
once took almost three years

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.460
where I made almost no content.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:18.340
So I hope that gives
everyone a sense of relief

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.200
that if you have a bad
week or even a bad month,

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.620
it doesn't mean the end
of your content career.

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.067
That's number one.

00:12:26.067 --> 00:12:29.320
Number two, notice what
I came back and did,

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.890
after five years of doing wine content

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.950
and not doing content for three years,

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:38.890
the content pillar that I
decided to do was a Q&amp;A format.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:40.040
Why did I do that?

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.500
Because I needed the audience

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.673
to be a contributor to
the content creation.

00:12:44.673 --> 00:12:46.010
I think one of the great mistakes

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:47.400
that a lot of people make

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.290
is they don't incorporate their audience

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.803
as a potential starter to creative.

00:12:53.946 --> 00:12:58.946
It is an amazing training
wheels set up, chess move,

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:06.300
putting you halfway home,
incorporating your audience

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.630
to being a starting point to more content

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:11.950
is something more people need to do.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:15.743
Q&amp;A's, answering questions, interactions.

00:13:17.403 --> 00:13:19.200
And then finally,

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.520
I'm a very big believer
in what I do with DRock,

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.640
like filming your day to day

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:27.330
is an incredible way to scale content.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.580
The other thing I did was I
did a ton of podcasts and shows

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.440
that had very small audiences

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:34.780
just to be on the
receiving end of questions,

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:36.230
so that I would have content.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:42.094
So literally DMing small
podcasts and saying, hey,

00:13:42.094 --> 00:13:44.310
if you'd like to interview me

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:47.170
and as you're evolving
through your career,

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.140
that's a good get for a small podcast,

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.030
so it's good for them,
but it's also good for you

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.843
'cause you can post, produce the creative,

00:13:53.843 --> 00:13:55.500
and what's amazing about Q&amp;A

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.916
is the questions take you to
places you won't take yourself.

00:13:58.916 --> 00:14:00.630
So those are some things to think about.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:04.300
I view that content is the oxygen

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:07.350
that creates awareness
around what you're doing.

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:11.550
So to your point, if you stop
creating to do something,

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.360
you in essence are turning off the oxygen

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.193
of what you're doing.

00:14:15.193 --> 00:14:18.760
So the reason I have
continuously content created,

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:23.560
even though I've gotten
remarkably busier in my time

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.480
is because I agree with that.

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:30.480
I think once you stop creating,
you become less vulnerable.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:35.020
Oprah Winfrey businesses
are not as impactful today

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:38.133
as they were a decade ago,
'cause she doesn't have a show.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:41.100
That's just real life.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:46.100
And so yeah, I'm a
believer that at all costs,

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.479
as a matter of fact,

00:14:48.479 --> 00:14:51.200
one of my biggest anxiety
points professionally is that

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.320
because now VeeFriends is so successful

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:58.230
and taking up my time, while
I still have to run VaynerX,

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:02.230
the thing that, we only have
so much time in the day,

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.040
the biggest casualty

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.963
to the huge success that I
have in NFT land is my content.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:12.750
I am definitely in a
different output place,

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:14.160
I mean, I went seven, eight years

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.250
without
(upbeat ambient music)

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.890
putting out four pieces of content

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.960
on my Instagram every day,
and now I get two a day

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.870
and that's like a big
day and that adds up.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:25.673
And so I'm conscious of
that, I think about that.

